---
export const prerender = true;

// About — the career narrative. Insight-first arc across 13 years, a short
// note on how Korab runs his own work, and a quiet close with contact links.
// Copy is disclosure-cleared per docs/plans/2026-07-03-console-mvp.md —
// do not add specifics (names, vendors, metrics, comp, transitions).

import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import portrait from "../assets/portrait-illustrated.jpg";
import portraitDay from "../assets/portrait-illustrated-day.jpg";
import SkillsSection from "../components/SkillsSection/SkillsSection.astro";
import StatusChip from "../components/StatusChip/StatusChip.astro";
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { readSkills } from "../lib/skills";
import { STATUS } from "../lib/status";

const skills = await readSkills();

const jsonLd = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "ProfilePage",
  "@id": "https://korabeland.com/about",
  url: "https://korabeland.com/about",
  name: "About · korab eland",
  description:
    "13 years across marketing, CX and operations. Now building the AI-driven kind.",
  mainEntity: { "@id": "https://korabeland.com/#person" },
};
---

<BaseLayout
  title="about · korab eland"
  description="13 years across marketing, CX and operations. Now building the AI-driven kind. The career arc, how I operate, and how to reach me."
  active="about"
>
  <script type="application/ld+json" slot="jsonld" set:html={JSON.stringify(jsonLd)} />

  <article class="about">
    <header class="about-header">
      <p class="t-label">§ · about</p>
      <h1 class="t-display about-title">Turning ambiguous problems into systems</h1>
    </header>

    <figure class="about-portrait">
      <Image
        class="portrait-night"
        src={portrait}
        alt="Illustrated portrait of Korab Eland"
        widths={[440, 880]}
        sizes="(max-width: 680px) 280px, 440px"
        loading="eager"
      />
      <Image
        class="portrait-day"
        src={portraitDay}
        alt="Illustrated portrait of Korab Eland"
        widths={[440, 880]}
        sizes="(max-width: 680px) 280px, 440px"
        loading="eager"
      />
      <figcaption class="t-mono about-portrait-cap">
        <span>korab eland</span>
        <span class="about-portrait-loc">{STATUS.targetReadout}</span>
      </figcaption>
    </figure>

    <section class="about-body" aria-labelledby="narrative">
      <h2 id="narrative" class="sr-only">Career narrative</h2>
      <p>
        The thread across thirteen years is the same one every time: take a problem
        nobody has fully framed yet, find the structure inside it, and build something
        that keeps running after I step back. The titles changed a lot more than the
        underlying work did.
      </p>
      <p>
        I started in digital media buying, running paid search and paid social
        campaigns and learning to read a dashboard for the decision hiding inside it.
        That pulled me into marketing, then into leading a marketing team, then into
        customer experience, each move widening the aperture from a channel to a
        funnel to the whole business. At Keypath Education I've spent over a decade
        moving through that arc: media buyer, digital media specialist, marketing
        manager, marketing and CX manager, and now CX manager for the Australian
        portfolio, working across admissions, marketing, paid media and data. Every
        step added a layer of the business I had to understand well enough to explain
        simply to the people making decisions in it.
      </p>
      <p>
        The constant underneath the titles is the same instinct: simplify complex
        strategy so people can actually act on it, and back decisions with evidence
        instead of hearsay. That instinct is what's pulling me toward AI now. I've led
        the evidence work behind a lead-scoring model that replaces fixed tiers with a
        proper probability score, aligning stakeholders across four functions before
        touching a line of the build. I've also run an end-to-end pilot on AI-driven
        SMS engagement, built on a randomised holdout so the result means something
        rather than something that just feels right.
      </p>
      <p>
        None of that is a pivot away from what came before. It's the same operating
        system, aimed at harder problems: frame it properly, find the evidence, build
        something that holds up once I'm not the one holding it together.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="about-operate" aria-labelledby="operate">
      <h2 id="operate" class="t-label">how I operate</h2>
      <p>
        I run my own work the same way I'd want a good system run: a backlog tied to
        actual goals, AI doing the first pass of triage, everything written down as
        plain markdown instead of trapped in someone's head. I wrote up the full
        system at
        {" "}
        <a href="/notes/system-designer-personal-os">/notes/system-designer-personal-os</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    {skills && <SkillsSection data={skills} />}

    <section class="about-close" aria-labelledby="close">
      <h2 id="close" class="sr-only">Contact</h2>
      <p class="t-mono about-status">
        <StatusChip status="available" variant="pulse" label="currently exploring ai / data / product roles" />
      </p>
      <p class="t-mono about-authorization">{STATUS.aboutLine}</p>
      <p class="t-mono about-links">
        <a href="mailto:korabeland@gmail.com">email</a> ·{" "}
        <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/korabeland" rel="me">linkedin</a> ·{" "}
        <a href="mailto:korabeland@gmail.com?subject=Resume%20request">resume available on request</a>
      </p>
    </section>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .about {
    max-width: 680px;
    margin-inline: auto;
    padding: var(--s-7) var(--s-4) var(--s-8);
  }

  .sr-only {
    position: absolute;
    width: 1px;
    height: 1px;
    padding: 0;
    margin: -1px;
    overflow: hidden;
    clip: rect(0, 0, 0, 0);
    white-space: nowrap;
    border: 0;
  }

  .about-header {
    margin: 0 0 var(--s-6);
  }

  .about-portrait {
    margin: 0 0 var(--s-7);
    max-width: 440px;
    border: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }

  .about-portrait img {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
  }

  /* Portrait tracks the shift: orange field by night (the no-JS default),
     blue by day. The day variant stays hidden until the head script sets
     data-time=day, mirroring the ShiftToggle idiom. */
  .about-portrait .portrait-day {
    display: none;
  }
  :global(html[data-time="day"]) .about-portrait .portrait-night {
    display: none;
  }
  :global(html[data-time="day"]) .about-portrait .portrait-day {
    display: block;
  }

  .about-portrait-cap {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: var(--s-3);
    padding: var(--s-2) var(--s-3);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }

  .about-portrait-loc {
    color: var(--signal);
  }

  @media (max-width: 680px) {
    .about-portrait {
      max-width: 280px;
    }
  }

  .about-header .t-label {
    display: block;
    margin: 0 0 var(--s-3);
  }

  .about-title {
    font-size: clamp(28px, 5vw, 40px);
    max-width: 18ch;
    color: var(--ink);
    margin: 0;
  }

  .about-body {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--s-4);
  }

  .about-body p {
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    margin: 0;
  }

  .about-operate {
    margin-top: var(--s-7);
    padding-top: var(--s-5);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }

  .about-operate .t-label {
    display: block;
    margin: 0 0 var(--s-3);
  }

  .about-operate p {
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    margin: 0;
  }

  .about-operate a {
    color: var(--ink);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-decoration-thickness: 1px;
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
  }

  .about-operate a:hover,
  .about-operate a:focus-visible {
    color: var(--signal);
  }

  .about-close {
    margin-top: var(--s-7);
    padding-top: var(--s-5);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--s-3);
  }

  .about-status {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    text-transform: none;
    letter-spacing: 0.02em;
  }

  .about-authorization {
    text-transform: none;
    letter-spacing: 0.02em;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    font-size: 13px;
    line-height: 1.5;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .about-links {
    text-transform: none;
    letter-spacing: 0.02em;
  }

  .about-links a {
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    text-decoration: none;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
    transition: color 150ms ease, border-color 150ms ease;
  }

  .about-links a:hover,
  .about-links a:focus-visible {
    color: var(--signal);
    border-bottom-color: var(--signal);
  }

</style>
